ially  come forward  while the star of the original Blade  series will not be returning for the MCU  reboot Wesley Snipes place in Marvel  history will never be forgotten Snipes  has had several encounters with law  enforcement but it wasn't until 2008  that the U.S Marshals actor had his  mugshot taken by none other than the U.S  Marshals service themselves after his  arrest the actor faced charges for  failing to file tax returns between 1999  and 2004. a period wherein he had  accrued nearly 40 million dollars though  he offered to pay approximately 842  thousand dollars of his 23 point million  dollar debt Snipes was fined 5 million  dollars and given a three-year prison  sentence according to people he was  released from prison in 2013 after which  he quickly resumed his acting career  appearing in films such as Chiraq  Dolomite is my name and coming to  America the latter film would see him  reprise his role from the 1980s cult  comedy classic Coming to America  starring Eddie Murphy in 2020 Snipes  rest re-entered the public Focus due to  the apparent hypocrisy of the US  government for not arresting former  president Donald Trump after accusations  of tax evasion the actor's arrest and  federal prison time were seen in a new  light with many people calling for  apologies to be made including author  Sam J Miller who wrote Wesley Snipes and  Lauren Hill had their careers destroyed  oh and they went to jail for failing to  pay taxes  the original Roadie to rdj's Tony Stark  Iron Man co-star Terence Howard has had  a tumultuous personal life the academy  award-nominated actor had his mugshot  captured twice both times related to an  assault on a woman in the year 2000  Howard was arrested after a flight  attendant accused him of grabbing her  during a disagreement surrounding the  fastened seatbelt sign according to ABC  News while charges were not pursued  after his 2000 arrest the details behind  his 2001 mug shot are a bit more complex  as cited by the Chica